Comment: 0,0:23:39.98,0:23:40.07,Default,chptr,0,0,0,,{Preview}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.54,0:01:44.33,Default,Oe,0,0,164,,I had a cat.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.88,0:01:47.13,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,Go on. {i think i should change this line} {not changing cause sam said so}
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.00,0:01:51.05,Default,Oe,0,0,164,,A police officer called out to me all of a sudden.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.05,0:01:53.76,Default,Oe,0,0,164,,Then there were two, then three.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.76,0:01:57.47,Default,Oe,0,0,164,,I thought, "If they take me in now, \Nmy cat is going to die."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.47,0:02:02.48,Default,Oe,0,0,164,,My place doesn't allow us to own pets, \Nso no one else knew about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.35,0:02:07.23,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,In March 2016, in Morioka City, Iwate Prefecture,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.69,0:02:13.03,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,a young girl and her mother \Nwere found stabbed to death in their home.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.61,0:02:21.41,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,The Morioka Prosecutor's Office indicted local resident \NOe Keita on charges of robbery and murder.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.87,0:02:24.42,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,The events leading to his arrest were thus:
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.42,0:02:28.84,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,Oe fled during questioning by patrol officers,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.84,0:02:31.21,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,and when they chased him into his home,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.21,0:02:35.01,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,they discovered a blade covered in blood,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.47,0:02:38.51,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,and arrested him on the spot. {CR: in flagrante delicto}
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.34,0:02:29.38,Default,Police,0,0,164,,{\an8}Hey! Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.81,0:02:41.06,Default,Police,0,0,164,,{\an8}There he is!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.06,0:02:41.85,Default,Police,0,0,164,,{\an8}Don't move!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.27,0:02:45.31,Default,Police,0,0,164,,{\an8}Stop resisting!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.81,0:02:45.31,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,DNA analysis later revealed that \Nthe blood on the blade matched the victims'.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.77,0:02:49.73,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,Oe consistently denied all culpability for the crime.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.73,0:02:52.24,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,On the blade collected as evidence, he insisted...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.24,0:02:53.78,Default,Oe,0,0,164,,I just picked it up.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.78,0:02:54.78,Default,Oe,0,0,164,,It wasn't mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.70,0:02:57.91,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,That's a bit of a stretch, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.91,0:03:01.95,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,I mean, if he ran away from the questioning, \Nhe must be hiding something, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.50,0:03:03.50,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,Not necessarily.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.50,0:03:09.46,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,He was previously a victim of wrongful questioning because an acquaintance of his had used drugs.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.46,0:03:11.88,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,You're saying that left him traumatized?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.88,0:03:14.30,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,Still, he just "picked it up"?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.30,0:03:17.47,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,A bloody kitchen knife? Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.93,0:03:21.10,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,He claims he was planning \Nto turn it in to the police later.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.10,0:03:22.31,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,Later?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.47,0:03:24.77,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.77,0:03:26.69,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,None of his claims hold up.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.10,0:03:29.40,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,However, when you consider Oe's background—
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.40,0:03:33.32,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,that he works as a live-in employee \Nat a non-profit organization—
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.32,0:03:35.70,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,it starts sounding plausible.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.07,0:03:38.11,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,A non-profit? What about it?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.87,0:03:44.58,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,They provide housing to elderly people \Nwith nowhere to go and help them live independently.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.58,0:03:47.92,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,Oe's job was taking care of the elderly there.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.50,0:03:51.17,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,However, they didn't pay him a wage.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.75,0:03:54.67,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,He received what they called an allowance, \Nsuch as on New Year's,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.67,0:03:57.68,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,and was given meals and groceries in kind.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.68,0:04:02.89,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,Despite that, they collected \N50,000 yen a month from him as rent.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.89,0:04:03.97,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,Brutal.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.43,0:04:08.06,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,Apparently, quite a few \Nof the residents have prior records.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.06,0:04:11.65,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,As for why he didn't immediately \Nturn in the weapon, he said...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.02,0:04:18.28,Default,Oe,0,0,164,,The rules say we can't call the cops or ambulances, \Nbecause they'd bother the neighbors.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.91,0:04:23.24,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,That organization sounds kinda shady, doesn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.24,0:04:26.62,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,Yeah. It's about as close to illegal as you can get.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.04,0:04:30.83,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,There's been an increase \Nin shady organizations in the region
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.83,0:04:34.42,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,ever since disaster relief funds started flowing.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.42,0:04:37.67,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,So it's not surprising \Na murder weapon was lying around. {wait how did he reach this conclusion?} {nice tl error}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.09,0:04:41.59,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,There's a good possibility Oe is innocent.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.18,0:04:46.47,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,First, we'll investigate \Nthe organization's activities and tax filings,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.47,0:04:49.35,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,then run background checks \Non all the residents.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.35,0:04:52.36,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,I'll focus on getting information out of Oe.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.36,0:04:54.15,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,You handle the investigation, Shimizu.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.15,0:04:57.74,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,You're dumping it on me just like that?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.61,0:05:01.28,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,Could you take care of his cat, too?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.28,0:05:02.37,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,The cat?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.87,0:05:07.20,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,{\i1}The commission for public defense cases is low, \Ndespite how much work they take.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.20,0:05:09.41,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,{\i1}The public is already set on a guilty verdict.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.41,0:05:12.12,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,{\i1}Plus, there's no suspended sentence in murder cases.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.12,0:05:13.92,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,{\i1}He might even get the death penalty.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.92,0:05:15.75,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,{\i1}There's nothing to gain here.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.09,0:05:19.09,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,Jeez, Higuruma{**-san}!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.09,0:05:21.97,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,Why'd you go and accept a case like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.97,0:05:23.97,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,It's fine from time to time.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.97,0:05:26.56,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,If we only take easy cases, we'll get rusty.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.56,0:05:29.02,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,{\i1}It's more like all the time!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.02,0:05:30.94,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,It's more like all the time!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.48,0:05:33.77,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,You're thinking out loud.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.15,0:05:39.11,Default,Takagi,0,0,164,,Sounds like Higuruma{**-kun} hasn't changed then. {this needs to be consistent two lines later}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.69,0:05:42.95,Default,Takagi,0,0,164,,It's rough when your boss isn't in it for the money.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.41,0:05:48.62,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,I mean, I'm not saying he should \Nrun a café on the side like you, Takagi{**-san}. {CR: At least it's not so bad that I'm being told to run a café on the side like you.}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.62,0:05:52.92,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,But when you say he hasn't changed, \Nyou mean he's always been like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.92,0:05:54.67,Default,Takagi,0,0,164,,Hm? Not really.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.29,0:05:57.96,Default,Takagi,0,0,164,,If anything, he's gotten worse. {CR: I think he actually used to be worse.} {crunchy... what are we doing here}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.96,0:05:58.88,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,No way...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.51,0:06:01.42,Default,Takagi,0,0,164,,Back when he was working with us,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.42,0:06:04.59,Default,Takagi,0,0,164,,he was in charge of a reckless driving case \Nwhere someone got hurt.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.59,0:06:06.93,Default,Takagi,0,0,164,,Oh, it was a drunk driving case.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.39,0:06:09.72,Default,Takagi,0,0,164,,The defendant was nineteen.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.72,0:06:14.44,Default,Takagi,0,0,164,,His coworkers pressured him into drinking and driving.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.44,0:06:17.27,Default,Takagi,0,0,164,,However, they all got their stories straight.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.27,0:06:21.90,Default,Takagi,0,0,164,,He couldn't pay for a settlement, \Nand we couldn't get his sentence suspended.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.53,0:06:28.66,Default,Client,0,0,164,,Liar!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.37,0:06:33.12,Default,Client,0,0,164,,You said they'd find me not guilty!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.96,0:06:40.50,Default,Takagi,0,0,164,,You said you'd get him a suspended sentence, though, \Nnot prove him innocent.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.09,0:06:42.84,Default,Takagi,0,0,164,,Have you learned your lesson now?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.84,0:06:46.05,Default,Takagi,0,0,164,,Quit taking on impossible cases. {hopeless criminal cases}
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.68,0:06:51.06,Default,Takagi,0,0,164,,Trying to save the weak may be a noble endeavor,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.06,0:06:56.60,Default,Takagi,0,0,164,,but there's only so much we lawyers can do\Nwithout support from the courts and prosecutors.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.35,0:06:57.44,Default,Girl,0,0,164,,{\an8}Oh, I wanna ride that!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.60,0:07:00.02,Default,Takagi,0,0,164,,It's not worth it when even your clients turn on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.98,0:07:06.16,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,They're at the end of their rope, \Nmentally and financially.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.61,0:07:08.99,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,I can't blame them for lashing out at me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.20,0:07:14.62,Default,Takagi,0,0,164,,And how are {\i1}you{\i0} holding up mentally, Higuruma{**-kun}?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.75,0:07:16.62,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.90,0:07:41.94,Default,Judge,0,0,164,,We find the defendant...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.32,0:07:43.48,Default,Judge,0,0,164,,not guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.74,0:07:50.66,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,We actually won?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.58,0:07:53.95,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,Not yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.29,0:07:57.42,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,They'll appeal right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.71,0:08:04.17,Default,Announcer,0,0,164,,{\i1}The prosecution has...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.43,0:08:17.81,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,None of the stolen items were found in your room.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.81,0:08:22.77,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,Another resident of the same organization \Nwent missing soon after the crime.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.77,0:08:31.49,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,{\q2}And the big one was you being caught on a convenience store \Nsecurity camera at the estimated time of the crime. {from the autopsy}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.49,0:08:34.70,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,Good thing you don't cook for yourself, Oe{**-san}!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.70,0:08:38.62,Default,Oe,0,0,164,,{*}Higuruma, sir{*Higuruma-sensei}, thank you so much. {CR: Counselor Higuruma} {clients don't typically say "Counselor" in casual conversation, "Sir" is what a grateful client would normally say}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.12,0:08:41.21,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,Please, no need to be so formal. {you can drop the honorifics.} {we've done this meme in s1, not again, besides it was played as a joke back then but this time it isn't}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.63,0:08:43.34,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,Besides, we're not in the clear yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.34,0:08:44.88,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,We still have the second trial.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.92,0:08:47.47,Default,Oe,0,0,164,,That's not what I mean.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.13,0:08:53.18,Default,Oe,0,0,164,,Thank you for believing me!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.56,0:09:07.32,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,While defense lawyers have to work \N\hwith limited budgets and manpower,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.32,0:09:11.49,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,prosecutors can pour manpower and \Ntaxpayer money into digging up evidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.49,0:09:14.24,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,That's fine. That's how the system works.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.24,0:09:19.66,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,However, in the second trial, \Nthe prosecutors presented no new evidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.42,0:09:27.51,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,Yet the court made the absurd finding that \Nthere was no reason to suspect the missing person,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.51,0:09:29.47,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,and the verdict was overturned.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.51,0:09:34.60,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,The Supreme Court is a narrow gate for a third trial.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.60,0:09:37.14,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,Most appeals are turned away at the door.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.14,0:09:40.06,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,It's hard to even get a proper hearing.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.02,0:09:44.73,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,This trial was set up \Nfor a guilty verdict from the start. {The system had branded him guilty from the start.} {a bit too strong} {deliberately rigged, not destined}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.78,0:09:56.91,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,{\i1}Why are you looking at me that way?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.62,0:10:03.75,Default,Takagi,0,0,164,,And how are {\i1}you{\i0} holding up mentally, Higuruma{**-kun}?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.71,0:10:09.09,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,I'm not trying to champion saving the weak.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.01,0:10:14.72,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,It's always been against my nature \Nto ignore something I knew was wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.30,0:10:17.72,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,It's just a part of me I cannot change.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.51,0:10:22.77,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,Lady Justice closes her eyes \Nto uphold equality under the law. {Lady Justice blindfolds herself \Nto uphold equality under the law.}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.77,0:10:26.56,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,People close their eyes \Nwhenever it benefits them. {People turn a blind eye \Nwhenever it benefits them.}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.15,0:10:31.69,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,Amidst all that, I don't want \Nthose reaching out for help to go unseen. {simpler and more relevant metaphor} {also why was that rant here?}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.24,0:10:38.20,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,At the very least, \NI want to keep my eyes open. {the close -> close -> open idea works in this version but not with the blind(fold) lines even tho they are better technically, preserving this idea is more important imo}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.20,0:10:49.63,Default,Judge,0,0,164,,If there are any objections to this ruling, \Nsubmit a petition for final appeal within fifteen days. {including today/starting today is kinda unnecessary}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.18,0:11:02.81,Default,Shimizu,0,0,164,,Higuruma{**-san}?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.44,0:11:08.48,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,Everyone, come back.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.40,0:11:15.57,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,We're having a retrial.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.28,0:11:20.53,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\pos(480,1015)}Higuruma is in...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.28,0:11:20.53,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\pos(1440,1015)}Higuruma is in...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.62,0:11:22.41,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\pos(480,1015)}Ikebukuro.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.53,0:11:21.62,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\pos(1440,1015)}Shinjuku.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.41,0:11:23.04,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\pos(480,1015)}Got it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.41,0:11:25.00,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Shinjuku?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.00,0:11:27.12,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}I hope Itadori is heading there, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.12,0:11:28.75,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Ikebukuro, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.75,0:11:30.34,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wonder if Fushiguro's there, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.42,0:11:37.01,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Isn't she a little late?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.01,0:11:43.43,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,When is that girl going to bring me my next sucker?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.56,0:11:53.28,Default,Bullies,0,0,164,,H-Hey, what was that?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.28,0:11:56.86,Default,Amai,0,0,164,,{\i1}Oh, no. Not like that. Not at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.86,0:11:59.49,Default,Bullies,0,0,164,,Hey, what're you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.99,0:12:01.37,Default,Amai,0,0,164,,{\i1}Do it exactly like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.37,0:12:03.29,Default,Bullies,0,0,164,,R-Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.29,0:12:04.87,Default,Amai,0,0,164,,{\i1}Why'd you go quiet?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.87,0:12:07.92,Default,Amai,0,0,164,,{\i1}Just keep grinning like an idiot!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.21,0:12:14.00,Default,Amai,0,0,164,,{\i1}See? What did I tell you?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.00,0:12:16.34,Default,Amai,0,0,164,,{\i1}Not that I actually told you anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.34,0:12:19.72,Default,Amai,0,0,164,,{\i1}Why don't you get it? Are you stupid?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.72,0:12:22.85,Default,Amai,0,0,164,,{\i1}These guys aren't smart or athletic.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.85,0:12:25.47,Default,Amai,0,0,164,,{\i1}Their pride is through the roof, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.47,0:12:27.48,Default,Amai,0,0,164,,{\i1}Just don't hurt their egos.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.48,0:12:30.69,Default,Amai,0,0,164,,{\i1}Keep grinning and play the fool.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.69,0:12:34.32,Default,Amai,0,0,164,,{\i1}Do that and no one else will target you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.32,0:12:36.94,Default,Amai,0,0,164,,{\i1}You might even get something nice out of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.87,0:12:06.58,Default,Bullies,0,0,164,,{\an8}Oh, come on!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.71,0:12:10.54,Default,Bullies,0,0,164,,{\an8}That's what you get!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.09,0:12:14.67,Default,Bullies,0,0,164,,{\an8}What? You got a problem, pal?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.67,0:12:15.80,Default,Bullies,0,0,164,,{\an8}Take that!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.49,0:12:38.99,Default,Yuji,0,0,164,,Cut it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.16,0:12:43.99,Default,Amai,0,0,164,,{\i1}Here comes another idiot.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.99,0:12:46.45,Default,Bullies,0,0,164,,Isn't that uniform from West Middle?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.45,0:12:48.25,Default,Bullies,0,0,164,,You're a middle schooler?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.25,0:12:50.83,Default,Bullies,0,0,164,,You gotta learn to watch your mouth, kid.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.83,0:12:53.46,Default,Bullies,0,0,164,,How about I teach you {\alpha&HFF&}a lesson!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.46,0:12:54.67,Default,Bullies,0,0,164,,How about I teach you a lesson!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.35,0:13:12.56,Default,Bullies,0,0,164,,Violence is bad!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.40,0:13:18.53,Default,Bullies,0,0,164,,Take this!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.41,0:13:30.62,Default,Yuji,0,0,164,,What about you?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.92,0:13:35.75,Default,Amai,0,0,164,,M-Me?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.96,0:13:37.76,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Hey.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.13,0:13:39.21,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.21,0:13:42.63,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,If you're planning to go to Shinjuku \Nthrough Ikebukuro, don't.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.05,0:13:44.93,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,That area's rich with supplies.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.43,0:13:47.64,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,We're bound to run into other players.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.10,0:13:50.64,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,There are two reasons for going this way.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.64,0:13:55.11,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,The route's easy to follow, and I have a base nearby.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.48,0:13:58.82,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,At least let me take a shower.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.82,0:14:01.53,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,I've barely rested since yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.45,0:14:07.49,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,Higuruma uses this theater as his base.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.49,0:14:09.45,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,Assuming he hasn't moved, that is.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.45,0:14:10.75,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Cool!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.75,0:14:13.21,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,You've been a big help! Thanks!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.71,0:14:16.46,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,Oh, h-h-hold on a sec!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.75,0:14:17.92,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.92,0:14:19.67,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,You're seriously going in?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.67,0:14:23.47,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,I'd rather reunite with my friend first, \Nbut we're in a hurry.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.93,0:14:26.51,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,I haven't met Higuruma myself,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.51,0:14:29.97,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,but he once beat Haba{**-san} to a pulp.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.97,0:14:31.73,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Oh, I'll be fine, then!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.73,0:14:35.27,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,I beat Propeller Head too,\Nso I should at least be able to run away.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.02,0:14:37.98,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Later, then!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.03,0:14:41.19,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\i1}Come on, say it!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.32,0:14:44.24,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\i1}You gotta tell him, man!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.78,0:14:46.95,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\i1}Tell him to stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.66,0:14:56.08,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm sorry, Itadori.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.17,0:15:01.59,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Higuruma?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.46,0:15:06.30,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Sorry to break it to you, but I'm Reggie.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.30,0:15:09.22,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,You've been played.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.72,0:15:14.60,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,Oh, my! What a face!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.60,0:15:16.90,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,I'm not scared at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.90,0:15:18.44,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,Just so you know, Reggie—
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.44,0:15:19.23,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Stop talking.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.11,0:15:28.12,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,What a waste of time.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.83,0:15:39.75,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Who's there?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.34,0:15:42.34,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,What are you doing over there?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.30,0:15:45.55,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Same question.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.30,0:15:52.01,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Have you ever taken a bath with your clothes on?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.01,0:15:53.10,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Nope.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.02,0:15:56.98,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,It feels better than you'd expect.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.65,0:16:00.65,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.69,0:16:04.53,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Back in elementary school,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.53,0:16:08.03,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I loved those swimming classes\Nwhere we had to swim in our uniforms.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.45,0:16:11.95,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,A lot of things don't seem to matter these days.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.95,0:16:16.58,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,So I've been trying things I always thought I shouldn't do.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.58,0:16:20.00,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Guess I've gone off the rails in my thirties.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.00,0:16:21.17,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Is that funny?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.79,0:16:23.67,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,It's kinda amusing.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.25,0:16:25.96,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,You're Higuruma, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.59,0:16:27.63,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Indeed I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.01,0:16:28.97,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,I wanna talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.97,0:16:31.93,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Wait, wait. Hold on.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.39,0:16:34.14,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I'm a lawyer.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.14,0:16:38.69,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Talking to me will incur a consultation fee \Nof 5,000 yen every half hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.69,0:16:39.52,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Uh...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.36,0:16:42.94,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I'm kidding.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.94,0:16:45.86,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I wanted to play the money-grubbing lawyer for once.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.94,0:16:48.36,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Oh...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.07,0:16:51.16,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Judging from his behavior so far...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.78,0:16:53.70,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,You have 100 points, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.37,0:16:56.62,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}He's not an incarnated sorcerer.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.04,0:17:00.00,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}He's a modern sorcerer \Nwhose technique has awakened!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.00,0:17:01.54,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}We can talk it out!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.54,0:17:03.38,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}There's room for negotiation!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.38,0:17:06.13,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Not bad. You pass.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.13,0:17:06.88,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.88,0:17:11.09,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,That {*}cursed beast{*shikigami} tells me all I need to know.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.09,0:17:12.64,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,You're strong.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.64,0:17:16.47,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,If you were weak, I'd just kill you \Nand be done with it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.47,0:17:18.89,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,But you're good. You should join us.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.89,0:17:21.94,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\i1}What? That wasn't part of the agreement!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.19,0:17:24.94,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,What are you getting at?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.94,0:17:28.65,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,How much do you know about the Culling Game?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.36,0:17:31.11,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,I know that it's a ritual.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.11,0:17:34.37,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,It uses the cursed energy \Nof the players inside the barriers
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.37,0:17:36.99,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,to ferry the people of Japan \Nto the other side,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.99,0:17:39.29,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,and turn them into something inhuman. {more intentional, eariler line felt like it's a side effect}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.91,0:17:42.33,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}I probably shouldn't bring up {*}Master Tengen{*Tengen-sama}.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.33,0:17:46.00,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Oh? Do you know Kenjaku, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.88,0:17:48.71,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}I knew there'd be one!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.30,0:17:51.76,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}A sorcerer connected to Kenjaku!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.63,0:17:54.93,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Uh, so, to be blunt,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.80,0:17:59.43,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,we want to put an end to the Culling Game.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.89,0:18:01.14,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Er, time out.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.14,0:18:05.02,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,When I say "put an end," I mean we want to \Nnullify the compulsory killing.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.02,0:18:08.98,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Please let us use your 100 points\Nto add a rule for that.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.48,0:18:11.45,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I'll be blunt, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.15,0:18:13.36,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I refuse.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.95,0:18:16.45,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Is that another joke?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.28,0:18:18.24,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.24,0:18:21.71,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I just sense potential in the Culling Game.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.25,0:18:24.17,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Sometimes the law is powerless.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.17,0:18:27.63,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,But what about the rules of the Culling Game?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.63,0:18:32.09,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,If the power I've been granted is real, \Nthen those rules must be too.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.09,0:18:36.60,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,What you just said about \Nusing the players' cursed energy?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.60,0:18:38.39,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,It's likely a misdirect. {CR: That's probably a bluff.}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.39,0:18:39.22,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.22,0:18:44.39,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Or rather, that's more of a secondary objective.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.39,0:18:46.36,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,I have three reasons to believe so.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.69,0:18:48.27,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,The number of players.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.27,0:18:50.23,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,The strength gap between players.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.23,0:18:51.86,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,And the rules of the barriers.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.36,0:18:59.87,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,If roughly 1,000 people were equally split up \Nacross the ten colonies, that would be 100 per colony. {why does he even bring up this comparison? is this supposed to hint at the total player count? or did he just pull the total count out of his ass to show us how simple division works?}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.87,0:19:06.88,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,But among the players are sorcerers like \NKashimo or Higuruma, who are a cut above the rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.88,0:19:10.84,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,These two alone have already taken out sixty sorcerers.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.84,0:19:14.38,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Each colony probably has a monster like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.93,0:19:20.14,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,So once only the strong remain, \Nthe Culling Game will reach a stalemate?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.85,0:19:22.64,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}I did sense that.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.14,0:19:25.31,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}The colony has been too quiet.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.60,0:19:27.02,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,It already has.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.02,0:19:30.07,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,At least here in Tokyo No. 1.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.07,0:19:33.94,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,On top of that, there's the teleportation \Nwhen people enter the colony.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.94,0:19:36.07,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,It serves to spread them out,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.07,0:19:40.78,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,but its main goal is likely to encourage \Nan early second awakening in modern sorcerers.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.78,0:19:43.33,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Some die during the process, as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.33,0:19:46.33,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,If he were really trying to use the players' cursed energy,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.33,0:19:51.59,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,he would want as many sorcerers as possible \Nto fight for as long as possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.59,0:19:54.17,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,No indictments. No prosecutions. {Imagine a world where no indictments or prosecutions are needed.} {imagine a world where this line gets more time...}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.17,0:19:56.43,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Instead of debating cases in court,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.43,0:20:00.47,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,what if those who broke the rules were punished \Nas if by the laws of physics?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.47,0:20:02.72,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Wouldn't that be wonderful?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.72,0:20:04.98,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I'll acknowledge there are issues \Nwith the current rules,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.98,0:20:08.31,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,but I want to observe the system \Nat the core of this game.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.31,0:20:10.81,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,It won't do for it to end too soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.81,0:20:16.57,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I'd especially love to witness the stripping of a technique \Nmentioned in Rules 2 and 8 at least once.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.99,0:20:20.32,Default,Shoko,0,0,164,,It's better for the rules \Nif being stripped means death, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.32,0:20:23.37,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,The Culling Game itself is a ritual.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.37,0:20:26.37,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,If we drag this out,\Neveryone in this country will die.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.37,0:20:27.83,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,That's nonsense.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.83,0:20:30.75,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,The Culling Game claims to be long-lasting.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.75,0:20:33.25,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yeah, I don't really get that part either!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.59,0:20:37.51,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Let me rephrase it, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.09,0:20:41.64,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Let me use your 100 points, Higuruma!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.72,0:20:46.68,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Have you ever killed someone \Nwho ticked you off?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.81,0:20:54.15,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,It feels better than you'd expect.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.19,0:20:56.53,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is that a {*}cursed beast{*shikigami}?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.53,0:20:59.28,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Higuruma has over 100 points.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.28,0:21:01.78,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}He might've killed twenty sorcerers already.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.28,0:21:05.70,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I can't jump in recklessly. I better hang back.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.70,0:21:08.75,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'll be ready to handle whatever he throws at me!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.33,0:21:11.79,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Domain Expansion:
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.67,0:21:14.71,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Deadly Sentencing.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.97,0:21:32.44,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,The bit in the rules about "long-lasting" \Nis just a cover for the real plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.65,0:21:34.40,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,0)}Mark my words.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.77,0:21:39.61,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Kenjaku is going to drop a bomb \Nwhen only the strongest remain.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.61,0:21:43.66,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,300)}Only then will the Culling Game \Nhave served its purpose.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.94,0:23:42.53,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\an8}Now, make your argument.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.53,0:23:43.57,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\an8}What happens if I'm judged guilty?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.57,0:23:44.74,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\an8}Judgeman, please begin.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.74,0:23:45.90,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\an8}You mean I can just lie?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.90,0:23:47.70,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\an8}You get one chance to make a statement.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.70,0:23:48.70,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\an8}I can't control my cursed energy!
